## Information-preserving intake contract

For each recovered field or artifact:

1. Bind source conversation, turn, card locator, outer hash, embedded path, child size/hash, and parent-child relationship.
2. Preserve the package bytes unchanged in quarantine.
3. Map to an existing native field or record an explicit no-fit state.
4. Record transform name/version/config hash, `DEPENDS_ON`, `INVARIANT_UNDER`, and invalidation scope.
5. Keep authority false before and after mapping.
6. Prove deterministic round-trip preservation.

Reject attempts to import package `physically_authorized` flags, float-only active lineage, proxy OAV, template rows as observations, inferred commercial formula truth, hedonic design scores, or package stock labels as ExactStockRef/PreparationReceipt authority.

## Approval-gated installation sequence

### I0 - Freeze and rollback

Recheck branch, HEAD, index tree, staged paths, and status. Create a fresh path-preserving PAX archive immediately before the first repository mutation. Materialize it into a short Windows long-path-safe restore root and replay every regular-file hash. Do not start mutation until restoration verification passes.

### I1 - Quarantine receipts

Reuse existing canonical receipts by exact SHA. Create at most one new authority-false receipt per new outer hash. Record external locator, size, SHA, root/member counts, embedded ledgers, graph state, child holds, source locators, and all blockers. Retain promotion false.

### I2 - Field matrix and ancestry projections

Add the eight recovered parents and their embedded identities to the existing P2.2 field/native matrix. Preserve dependency semantics. Create only immutable project-design ancestry and typed authority-false candidate projections.

### I3 - Narrow native changes only if a real gap is proven

Expected result is no schema migration. Extend an existing adapter or read-only projection only when the field matrix and round-trip test prove information loss. P6 remains excluded until exact parents exist.

### I4 - Verification

Run focused receipt/scanner tests, field mapping and round-trip tests, C10/P3/C0/Laboratory Beta integration tests, V5 stock/product-basis negative tests, and the quick project verifier. Run full release verification only for a later release claim.

Required negatives: unknown stock strength, stale parent hashes, package stock-label promotion, template-row import, missing expected-cell coverage, product-basis active-fraction inference, proxy-OAV promotion, credential leakage, and any authority-bit flip.

### I5 - Acceptance receipt

Seal exact inputs, local changes, tests, rollback archive, final hashes, and remaining holds. Implementation completion does not create formula, inventory, stock, bottle, physical, sensory, OAV, safety, procurement, publication, or release authority.

